  "data_abstract": "The centrality dependence of strange ($\\rm K^{0}_{\\mathrm S}$, $\\Lambda+\\bar{\\Lambda}$) and multi-strange ($\\Xi^{-}+\\bar{\\Xi}^{+}$, $\\Omega^{-}+\\bar{\\Omega}^{+}$) hadron production is measured by ALICE in lead$-$lead (Pb$-$Pb) collisions at a centre-of-mass energy per nucleon pair of $\\sqrt{s_{\\mathrm{NN}}}=5.02~\\mathrm{TeV}$, using the full data set collected during LHC Run 2 (2015 and 2018). This is the largest heavy-ion data set analysed to date at the LHC and it allows for the extraction of transverse-momentum ($p_{\\mathrm T}$) spectra and $p_{\\mathrm T}$-integrated yields with unprecedented precision over a broad range of charged-particle multiplicity densities ($\\langle dN_{\\mathrm{ch}}/d\\eta\\rangle_{|\\eta|<0.5}$), probing regions where results from smaller collision systems (pp and p$-$Pb) are also available. The $p_{\\mathrm T}$ spectra evolve with centrality, featuring larger $\\langle p_{\\mathrm T}\\rangle$ in central events for all particles. The $\\Lambda/\\rm K^{0}_{\\mathrm S}$ ratio exhibits the distinctive baryon-to-meson enhancement in the intermediate-$p_{\\mathrm T}$ region, with a maximum that shifts to larger $p_{\\mathrm T}$ for more central collisions. The hadron-to-pion yield ratios are presented as a function of $\\langle dN_{\\mathrm{ch}}/d\\eta\\rangle_{|\\eta|<0.5}$ and compared to results from different collision systems and energies. A smooth connection from pp to Pb$-$Pb is observed, demonstrating that collision system or energy do not play a role in the multiplicity evolution of this observable. The previously reported enhancement of strangeness production in the multiplicity range probed in pp and p$-$Pb collisions saturates in the multiplicity range of the Pb$-$Pb data. These results constitute a key test bench for theoretical models, and a first comparison to the EPOS 4 generator is presented.",
